// Pull request: #5700 macOS process create detections related to Bluenoroff macOS intrusion
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5700
// Pull request author: stuartjash
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Remoted Spawning Shell
// Sigma ID: 4f03f395-a192-468f-8e4e-9cb8efd97b80
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Stuart Ashenbrenner
// Date: 2026-09-30 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.004, stealth, T1036.005
// Description: Detects the 'remoted' binary, a binary masquerading by living in the Library directory, spawning
//   a shell or osascript in order to execute an AppleScript payload. This technique was reported by
//   TA444 in the BlueNoroff macOS intrusion set.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration scripts shipped by a remoted web server in /Library/WebServer
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/inside-bluenoroff-web3-intrusion-analysis
//   - https://atomicredteam.io/execution/T1059.004/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ae9128c7ebd868a0d436fa9897f05d275ef26207/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_remoted_spawning_shell.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "/Library/WebServer" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/remoted") and (FolderPath endswith "/sh" or FolderPath endswith "/bash" or FolderPath endswith "/zsh" or FolderPath endswith "/osascript")
